From 4c7a9605be04dbcd8bdcad76c29a5a789cdf9311 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Olaoluwa Osuntokun <laolu32@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 10:20:46 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] compiler: make cache output reproducible

In this commit, we serialize unordered cache collections in key order and stabilize the traversal that allocates imported type IDs. Equal module interfaces, diagnostic names, Unicode source mappings, and local package manifests can otherwise produce different bytes between clean builds. Inline metadata also carries unordered parameter membership and record labels.

We preserve the existing serde wire shapes and runtime hash randomization. The regression tests cover equivalent maps and sets, type-ID remapping, standard-library inlining, diagnostic names, and Git package state. The core and CLI suites pass, and five cold builds of the complete Loom code-mode seed produce identical cache, Erlang, and BEAM files while warm builds reuse the caches.
